      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The skill declares no tool scope (permissions or allowed-tools) but contains code examples that perform file read and write operations (e.g., opening PDF files for reading, writing merged PDFs). This violates the principle of least privilege. While file operations are necessary for PDF processing, the lack of explicit scope declaration means the skill might be granted excessive file access (if the platform defaults to allow) or denied necessary access (if the platform defaults to deny). In a shared or multi-user environment, this could lead to unauthorized file access or skill failure.",
      "remediation": "Add a tool scope declaration in the skill's metadata to explicitly request the minimum required file permissions. For example, if the platform uses a 'permissions' field, include: permissions: [file_read, file_write]. This ensures the skill is granted only the necessary access and adheres to security best practices.",
      "code_snippet": null,
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "ASI02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "SQP-2",
      "finding_id": "finding-8099c7642b1e4ebdbf4ea9c4399be4d6",
